data: {"text":"1. That the Petitioner herein above named apprehends arrest in connection with FIR No. 142/2026"}

data: {"text":" dated 18.04.2026 registered at Police Station Doranda, Ranchi under Sections 318(4) and 336(3) of the"}

data: {"text":" Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023. The Petitioner has not been arrested yet but has reasonable"}

data: {"text":" apprehension of arrest based on the registration of the aforesaid FIR and therefore approaches this Hon"}

data: {"text":"'ble Court seeking anticipatory bail.\n\n2. That the Petitioner apprehends arrest in connection with FIR No. 142/2026 dated 18.04.2026 lodged at Police Station Doranda, Ranchi."}

data: {"text":" The said FIR has been registered against the Petitioner based on a completely false, frivolous and malicious complaint filed"}

data: {"text":" by the de-facto complainant who is known to the Petitioner.\n\n3. That the present case arises out of a commercial partnership"}

data: {"text":" dispute involving a transport business between the Petitioner and the de-facto complainant. The dispute is purely of civil nature pertaining to business"}

data: {"text":" transactions and settlement of accounts between the parties. The de-facto complainant, with malicious intent and"}

data: {"text":" to pressurize the Petitioner, has misused the criminal law by"}

data: {"text":" filing a false complaint.\n\n4. That the Petitioner is a well-known and respected transporter in Ranchi with an impeccable reputation"}

data: {"text":" in the business community. The Petitioner has no criminal antecedents whatsoever and has never been involved in any criminal activity. The Petitioner undert"}

data: {"text":"akes to cooperate fully with the investigation and commits not to leave the territorial jurisdiction of Jharkhand without prior permission of this Hon'ble Court.\n\n5. That the Petitioner has been fals"}

data: {"text":"ely implicated in the present case due to the commercial dispute with the de-facto complainant. The allegations"}

data: {"text":" leveled against the Petitioner are completely baseless and have been made with ulterior motives to har"}

data: {"text":"ass and humiliate the Petitioner. The dispute between the parties is purely civil in nature and does not warrant invo"}

data: {"text":"king criminal provisions.\n\n6. That the alleged offences are the result of a business dispute which"}

data: {"text":" is civil in nature and should be adjudicated in a civil court rather than being converted"}

data: {"text":" into a criminal matter. The de-facto complainant is trying to use criminal law as a tool to recover"}

data: {"text":" alleged dues which is an abuse of the process of law.\n\n7. That the Petitioner has"}

data: {"text":" deep roots in the community and has been residing at the same address in Ranchi for several years. The Petitioner has substantial business interests in"}

data: {"text":" Jharkhand and owns immovable properties in the state. There is no question"}

data: {"text":" of the Petitioner absconding or evading the process of law.\n\n8. That the Petitioner is ready and"}

data: {"text":" willing to join the investigation and cooperate with the investigating agency. The custodial interrogation of the Petitioner is not necessary as the Petitioner undertakes to make"}

data: {"text":" himself available for interrogation as and when required by the investigating officer during the course of investigation.\n\n9. That the fundamental"}

data: {"text":" right to life and personal liberty guaranteed under Article 21 of the Constitution of India includes the right to be free from arbitrary arrest and detention. The Hon"}

data: {"text":"'ble Supreme Court in numerous judgments has held that anticipatory bail is a valuable right"}

data: {"text":" which should be exercised judiciously to prevent abuse of the criminal justice system.\n\n10. That in the case"}

data: {"text":" of Sushila Aggarwal v. State (2020) 5 SCC 1, the Hon'ble Supreme Court has laid down the parameters"}

data: {"text":" for granting anticipatory bail and held that the court should consider factors like the nature of accusation, the ant"}

data: {"text":"ecedents of the applicant, the possibility of the applicant fleeing from justice and the likelihood of the applicant tamp"}

data: {"text":"ering with evidence.\n\n11. That considering the facts and circumstances of the present case, the nature of allegations, the clean ant"}

data: {"text":"ecedents of the Petitioner, his roots in the society, and his willingness to cooperate with the investigation,"}

data: {"text":" the Petitioner is entitled to the protection of anticipatory bail. The Petitioner undertakes to abide by any"}

data: {"text":" conditions that this Hon'ble Court may deem fit to impose while granting anticipatory bail.\n\n12. That the investigation"}

data: {"text":" is pending and no useful purpose would be served by arresting the Petitioner, particularly when the Petitioner has given"}

data: {"text":" an undertaking to cooperate with the investigation and has no intention to abscond or tam"}

data: {"text":"per with evidence. The liberty of the Petitioner should not be curtailed unnecessarily when the same"}

data: {"text":" can be protected by granting anticipatory bail with appropriate conditions."}

